# PLACEHOLDER: replace this whole file with the certificate chain of the grimalkin
# Windows code signing certificate once the CA has issued it.
#
# Contents: PEM certificates, leaf (the signing certificate) FIRST, then each
# intermediate CA, in order. Do not include the root and never a private key
# (the key lives in AWS KMS and cannot be exported). For example:
#
#   cat leaf.pem intermediate.pem > installer/windows/codesign-chain.pem
#
# While this file contains no "BEGIN CERTIFICATE" block, the release pipeline
# refuses to sign (when WINDOWS_SIGNING_ENABLED=true) and builds unsigned
# otherwise. CI checks that the leaf's public key is the KMS key's public key and
# its Subject equals the WINDOWS_SIGNING_PUBLISHER variable, and verifiers pin the
# issuer to the second certificate here. To renew (certificates last at most 460
# days), replace the file in a reviewed PR and update WINDOWS_SIGNING_PUBLISHER
# if the subject changed. See scripts/aws/README.md and docs/SIGNING-AWS.md.
